<section>

 
    <section>
        <header>
            <h1>Just Buttons</h1>
        </header>
        <article>
            <p>
                Explore the simplicity and elegance of buttons in their purest form with <strong>Just HTML</strong>. This section showcases a variety of button styles and functionalities, all created using basic HTML and Bootstrap. From classic primary buttons to interactive elements, discover how buttons can enhance user experience without the need for complex code.
            </p>
        </article>
        <article>
            <h2>What You'll Find</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Primary Button</strong>: The standard button style with a bold look.</li>
                <li><strong>Alert Button</strong>: An interactive button that triggers an alert message.</li>
                <li><strong>Link Styled as Button</strong>: A hyperlink styled to look like a button, blending form with functionality.</li>
                <li><strong>Outline Button</strong>: A sleek button style with an outline border.</li>
                <li><strong>Block Button</strong>: Full-width buttons that span the entire line.</li>
                <li><strong>Disabled Button</strong>: Buttons that are visually distinct and cannot be clicked.</li>
                <li><strong>Button Group</strong>: A cohesive group of buttons displayed inline.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Each button demonstrates the versatility and power of HTML combined with Bootstrap, proving that sometimes, less is more.
            </p>
        </article>
    </section>
    
    <hr style="border: 1px solid;">
